    63	
    64	## Lessons from the reference (requirements)
    65	
    66	| # | Lesson (reference evidence) | Where it lands |
    67	|---|---|---|
    68	| L1 | Evaluation must decide wins by raw final banks, not shaped return (a .8 economic cap could invert the real winner) | 3.2 |
    69	| L2 | Artificial truncation keeps the real economic reward earned on that transition and adds the critic bootstrap | 3.2 |
    70	| L3 | Rank seed streams use `seed+rank` with stride `world_size` on every reset (a `rank*n_envs` offset collided) | 1.4 |
    71	| L4 | Vendoring the engine turns on `serde_json/arbitrary_precision` for the whole crate, which breaks a test-only float decode in Isaiah's `src/rules_engine/generation.rs` fixtures | 1.1 |
    72	| L5 | A 4,096-game rank-0 evaluation exceeded the 600 s NCCL broadcast; Isaiah's cadence (128 envs/rank) avoids it, and idle GPUs during evaluation are not a hang | 3.3, 6.x |
    73	| L6 | An unresolved CUDA illegal memory access appeared in the BC-initialized rollout, surfacing at `_check_flags`; suspects are a dense-state index overflow and async host→device copies from overwritten native buffers | 0.2, 1.4, 2.3 |
    74	| L7 | W&B marks crashed runs "finished", and cleanup delays the traceback | 0.3 |
    75	| L8 | Self-play collapsed to zero banks through market behavior; BC bootstraps from public replays | Phase 5 |
    76	| L9 | BC overfit after about 14.6k updates (held-out NLL 0.761 → 1.954); select by held-out NLL | 5.2 |
    77	| L10 | The 4096 / spm 1 / accumulation 2 cadence ran 2,048 optimizer steps per iteration against Isaiah's 16 | 3.4 |
    78	| L11 | Muon exclusions and FlashAttention differed from Isaiah; both follow automatically from his classes and preset | 2.1, 3.4 |
    79	| L12 | Every evaluation reused one seed | 3.3 |
    80	| L13 | The flat features lost inventory insertion order and some public configuration facts | 1.3 |
    81	| L14 | Heavy local runs overloaded the owner's Mac | Global Constraints |
    82	| L15 | Component speed ≠ end-to-end speed; the async-GPU error surfaced far from its cause | 6.x run statements |
    83	
    84	## Isaiah's principles (from his `AGENTS.md`, `README.md`, config headers and `docs/model-architecture.md` at `32b3ec9`)
    85	
    86	| # | Principle | Kaggriculture form | Tasks |
    87	|---|---|---|---|
    88	| I0 | Stateless transformer: one encode per current observation, no hidden state, named token sequence, `evaluate_actions` returns log-probs, entropy and values from one encode, stateless teachers | Same | 2.x, 4.x |
    89	| I0b | **Same layer topology:** `ObservationInputStem` stems (hidden `embed_dim·mlp_ratio`); separate per-role token parameters (player, board scratch, actor plan, per-player critic value); `TransformerBlock` trunk and final LayerNorm; `OutputProjectionMLP` critic head per critic-value token; `3D → D` actor input projection over [entity, player, plan] | Same classes. Categorical fields enter the stems as one-hot channels; only channel widths and the grammar action heads are game-specific | 2.1–2.3 |
    90	| I1 | 16 optimizer steps per iteration; `spm × grad_accum` = 16; the split comes from a memory smoke ("grad_accum only as needed") | Start at spm 8 / accum 1 on 2 ranks; the smoke may move to 4 / 2 | 3.4, 6.1 |
    91	| I2 | The same global config on any hardware: divide per-rank `n_envs` and spm by world size | 2 × 128, 4 × 64 envs | 3.4 |
    92	| I3 | The LR schedule is defined over env steps; a batch change rescales warmup and decay | Any forced deviation rescales them in the YAML | 3.4, 6.1 |
    93	| I4 | Model ladder: GELU, `mlp_ratio 2.0`, `head_dim 32`, scale width×depth; 6m = 256×6 (5,679,118 params in Orbit) | Our trunk sits on the ladder | 2.4 |
    94	| I5 | Winner-distribution critic (value 2p − 1, gamma 1), value distillation on winner probabilities | Per-seat (self, opponent) softmax from the seat's own observation | 2.2 |
    95	| I6 | Last-best teacher: KL(teacher ‖ student), small coefficients, the teacher shares the student's architecture and is refreshed in place, cached path bit-for-bit equal to the combined path | Per-slot categorical KL over the grammar heads | Phase 4 |
    96	| I7 | Eval against last best, 70% promotion, separate current/best checkpoints, 8 replays exported | Raw-bank winners; Kaggriculture replay format | 3.3, 7.3 |
    97	| I8 | Throughput defaults: compiled GAE/loss, trunk `max-autotune-no-cudagraphs`, BF16, TF32, forced FlashAttention | Verified active in Phase 6 | 3.4, 6.x |
    98	| I9 | Parity-first engine; `docs/rules-parity-coverage.md` is the source of truth | Kaggriculture parity documented the same way | 1.1, 7.5 |
    99	| I10 | Docs are contracts: read the mapped doc first, update it with the change, `just docs-fresh` | Same | all |
   100	| I11 | Refactor rather than add compatibility shims; fail fast; strict persisted schemas; `isinstance` narrowing instead of `getattr` | Same | all |
   101	| I12 | `just py-prepare` / `rs-prepare` / `prepare`, `uv add` / `cargo add`, tracked lockfiles, PR checklist, merge commits | Same | all |
