     3	Read-only source review, 2026-09-29. File identities/excerpts are retained in this
     4	directory. This is not a new engine-parity execution or a learner result.
     5	
     6	## Execution and dependence
     7	
     8	`engine_rs/src/lib.rs`:
     9	
    10	- 1459–1499: own worker actions, market, town consumption, crop decay, daily
    11	  maintenance/reset, step increment and terminal cash outcome. Default episode
    12	  length 720 produces 719 transitions under the inspected stopping condition.
    13	- 1546–1579: count all submitted PLANT demands before worker execution; a crop
    14	  exceeding initial seeds has every request converted to PASS. Count failed-site
    15	  requests too. A prefix simulator cannot simply deduct successfully used seeds.
    16	- 1588–1625: farmer then hands in ordinal order; earlier tile/inventory effects
    17	  are visible to later workers. There is no free worker-order permutation.
    18	- 3142–3155: cardinal movement obeys bounds, not occupancy/locked-tile rules.
    19	- 3166–3187: DROP at shed access deposits in inventory insertion order, discards
    20	  overflow. 3190–3214: PICKUP fills from current shed stock, omitted amount one;
    21	  worker carrying capacity is not checked.
    22	- 3217–3257: PLACE animal into a compatible empty structure first; otherwise
    23	  deposit to shed up to room, retaining excess. Animal branch ignores quantity.
    24	- 3260 onwards: shed transfers occur before locked-tile guard. PLANT requires
    25	  empty tile at execution. WATER, HARVEST, FERTILIZE, DIG, BUILD, FEED, CARE and
    26	  COLLECT_FERTILIZER update shared tiles and the acting worker's inventory.
    27	- 3800–3842: HIRE cost is multiplier times Fibonacci(hires_today); successful
    28	  hires change cash/count and spawn at least-occupied shed access. 3845 onwards:
    29	  land unlock order NE/SW/SE and escalating prices.
    30	- 3869–3931: SELL uses shed only; price-one sale pays without adding market
    31	  inventory. Product/animal buys use shed room, seed buys use separate storage.
    32	  Market inventory is a price input, not a nonnegative supply admission rule.
    33	- 3959–4140: market positions run in order across players; HIRE/LAND before
    34	  merchandise in a position; per-unit quotes for both players are computed before
    35	  either commit. Orders may partially fill; subsequent quotes/cash are uncertain
    36	  without rival submissions. EMPTY consumes a position, STOP terminates.
    37	- 4204–4329, 4431–4528: maintenance and production, automatic deposits with
    38	  overflow, reset worker positions/inventories, remove hired hands, random weeds
    39	  and shop selection. A last-hour hire cannot act before disappearing.
    40	
    41	Valid chains can include DIG→PLANT, one-shot HARVEST→PLANT, PLANT→WATER,
    42	FERTILIZE→WATER, WATER→HARVEST, BUILD→animal PLACE→FEED/CARE, and ordered shed
    43	transfer chains. Multiple workers may need the same tile. Other workers can
    44	also undo a plan, so a selected-seed allocator is not a complete turn resolver.
    45	
    46	All workers precede market: DROP→SELL and SELL→BUY/HIRE are possible; buying a
    47	seed/new worker/land does not enable an earlier worker command this turn. Goods
    48	deposited at day end cannot be sold in the already-finished market phase.
    49	
    50	## Legal information boundary
    51	
    52	`engine_rs/src/myolie_features.rs` contains the current two-seat 8176-float
    53	encoding. It exposes own seeds/shed/per-worker inventories, both public tile and
    54	worker fields, public cash/markets/shops, and clock/hiring/land/capacity suffixes.
    55	The other seat's separate row contains private data and is prohibited input.
    56	
    57	The encoding is not lossless: item insertion order is absent; scaled bank/stock
    58	values become f32; some public custom market/config fields are omitted. Exact
    59	shadow execution requires an explicitly versioned legal current-state contract,
    60	not unrestricted access to `Game`. The selected proposal uses learned command
    61	coordination and does not introduce a hidden-state simulator in the actor.
    62	
    63	Even with exact own-state input and the full own program, market settlement and
    64	future random maintenance are not exactly known. No current-observation-only
    65	architecture can guarantee every contingent purchase fills while retaining all
    66	useful sale-funded actions and opponent privacy.

